TI  - E-SAFAR (Electronic Safe Journey Management System)
PY  - 2025
T2  - Society of Petroleum Engineers - SPE Conference at Oman Petroleum and Energy Show, OPES 2025
DO  - 10.2118/224858-MS
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105006906914?origin=resultslist
AD  - OQ Exploration and Production, Muscat, Oman
AB  - Journey Management is a commonly used process, particularly in the energy sector, to minimize the possibility and consequences of Motor Vehicle Incidents (MVI). Motor Vehicle Incidents often have underlying causes such as non-compliance with road safety regulations and procedures, unqualified drivers, Inappropriate vehicles, and inadequate evaluation of the road, environmental and climatic conditions. As a result, managing journeys from planning through execution till reaching the destination safely with proper and official closing the journey is crucial to ensure employee and assets safety. In line with its commitment to improving road safety, OQ Exploration and Production (OQEP) launched a comprehensive road safety strategy in 2023, extending through 2025. This strategy is built based on three core pillars: Engineering, Education, and Enforcement. A central feature of this strategy is the introduction of E-Safar, an advanced Electronic Journey Management System. E-Safar is designed to enhance journey planning, driver and vehicle management, and provides a centralized platform that integrates with both web-based and mobile applications, making it accessible on both Android and iOS devices. E-Safar replaces outdated paper-based systems, addressing the need for multilingual support with an icon-based interface in four languages: English, Arabic, Hindi, and Urdu. This design ensures that workers from diverse linguistic backgrounds can easily interact with the system. The platform provides real-time notifications, a reminder system, offering users instant updates on journey statuses, ensuring both driver safety and operational efficiency. Copyright 2025, Society of Petroleum Engineers.
