TI  - MobRec: Mobile platform for decentralized recommender systems
PY  - 2021
T2  - T-Labs Series in Telecommunication Services
SP  - 131
EP  - 164
DO  - 10.1007/978-3-030-68840-0_11
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85105046410?origin=resultslist
AD  - Technische Universität Berlin, Berlin, Germany
AB  - In this chapter, we develop a mobile platform for decentralized recommender systems—MobRec. The core concept is that everything runs on smartphones. Due to decentralization, MobRec does not exhibit the lock-in effects present in centralized service providers for recommender systems. In MobRec, ratings and preferences are captured locally. During daily life, these ratings and preferences are exchanged with users in proximity in a device-to-device manner. Locally running recommender systems or third-party service providers can then recommend items based on own data and data received from users met before. We implement the platform for off-the-shelf smartphones for both Android and iOS. We implement device-to-device data exchange that can run in the background on both platforms. In our evaluation, we show the feasibility of our approach. Our implementation can serve as a blueprint for future research and software development in this field. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2021.
